///| cmd/wasm_rng_probe -- Loop #84: what the wasm backend does when it has
///| no entropy to give.
///
///|   `src/rng`'s wasm backend has no entropy source: a bare wasm module has
///|   no operating system underneath it, no Web Crypto API and no host to
///|   ask.  The package's answer is to REPORT that, and this driver is how
///|   that answer is observed from the outside.
///
///|   It prints one line before the draw and one after.  On a target with an
///|   entropy source, both lines appear.  On the wasm backends, only the
///|   first one does -- the draw aborts, and the abort is the answer: a
///|   client handed zeros would use them as a key, and a zero key is not a
///|   key.
///
///|   The driver is wasm-only, and says so in its `moon.pkg`, because a
///|   `cmd/` package is a leaf: nothing imports it, so a package-level
///|   declaration costs nothing and makes the toolchain refuse the other
///|   targets instead of failing there with a confusing [4067].
import {
  "openssh/openssh_moonbit/src/rng",
}

pkgtype(kind: "executable")

options(
  supported_targets: "+wasm",
)
